1.What is Ensemble Learning in Machine Learning?
Ensemble learning is a machine learning technique where multiple models(weak learners) are trained and combined
to solve the same problem in order to get better accuracy,stability and robustness.

2.Why do we use multiple models instead of relying on a single Machine Learning model?
A single model may overfiy or underfit the data. Different model capture different patterns, combining them helps
balance bias and variance. Ensembles are more robust and generalize better to unseen data.

3.What is meant by a base learner or base estimator?
A base learner is an individual model that contributes to the ensemble.
Eg Decision Tree, Logistic Regression,
Each base learner makes predications and the ensemble combine them (averaging or voting).


4.What is the main idea behind Ensemble Learning?
The main idea is "wisdom of the crowd"
Just as a group of people can make better decisions collectively, multiple models can produce more accurate
predications together than one model alone.

